Notebook[{
Cell["A formal semantics for QuantumFramework", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"782f5365-32eb-4ad5-85a5-99c2ea2a7564"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This document describes QuantumFramework (QF) 2.1.1 (kernel ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "d3c29e8"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4e61cb45-0793-4398-ae16-41d9efffe2b4"],
 ", 2026-09-22). Sections 1 to 11 cover the finite-dimensional core: for each \
object, what QF stores, and what QF does with the stored information for each \
operation. The appendices hold the full nesting and return-head tables (A), \
the constructor edge cases (B), the phase-space formulas (C), and the \
placement against the published literature (D, the only part that cites)."
}], "Text",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"0ca60653-3dc4-4b49-9c77-b548b19f3cb8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One idea runs through the whole account: ",
 StyleBox["QF represents states and transformations together with their bases \
and subsystem structure, and then uses that information to compose them, \
discard subsystems, and read out measurements.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A single running example carries it: one object whose meaning comes from \
its declared basis, not from its stored coefficient array alone."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"eb217e90-3745-47c3-a0b9-138cf1d72766"],

Cell["1. States and operators", "Section",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"ed821ec4-dc4a-4a24-a1b6-e83c664533c6"],

Cell["\<\
A QuantumFramework state, operator, channel, or measurement is a coefficient \
array together with the information needed to read it. That information is \
what makes the array mean something, so it comes first: the array alone does \
not fix what it represents.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"1c3d03bf-e787-4871-955a-809b1dba320d"],

Cell["Take six complex numbers. The same six can be", "Text",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"66512c92-dc9d-4b20-ba91-5907f3ce23f1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "one six-level system, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"c1", ",", " ", "...", ",", " ", "c6"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "6"}], 
   "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ff6c0c8-4c34-411a-8d84-6038668637bf"],
 ", a qudit of dimension six;"
}], "Item",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"b1488c7f-e0c3-4b71-a4b3-0ea5d4eedb59"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "a qubit together with a qutrit, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"c1", ",", " ", "...", ",", " ", "c6"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e76189c2-4182-4ed8-be0a-133ce02b1024"],
 ";"
}], "Item",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"0e75c595-acd9-45aa-8a82-421fe74045fa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "a linear map from a qutrit to a qubit, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1142b717-cfbf-4746-ac69-0a8a2250b828"],
 " matrix with rows ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "2"], ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "3"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e9c1d8f-6f4f-4c47-94d4-70f387d390f8"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "4"], ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "5"], ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "6"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "241f01c9-9d50-48bb-8cbc-d48da434c449"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"c1", ",", " ", "c2", ",", " ", "c3"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"c4", ",", " ", "c5", ",", " ", "c6"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57814770-f8ab-481a-aee8-7b883e71f610"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"00a778f4-8910-4305-aa85-e5d23f8ac8db"],

Cell["\<\
Nothing in the numbers chooses among these. The subsystem dimensions and the \
split into what the object takes in and what it puts out decide it, and QF \
stores exactly that: for each object, the dimensions of its subsystems, an \
output side, an input side, and the basis on each side.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"67dcbae4-f308-4a2d-aa9d-c61045fd3e4f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The third reading, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "784f461a-8634-4f08-b140-6ef0b9795e38"],
 " map, lowers dimension from three levels to two. One physical operation has \
exactly this shape: removing a photon applies the annihilation operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["a", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "89318454-ad37-449a-819b-85764af8461f"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
    TemplateBox[{
      RowBox[{
        StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "1"}]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "afe86e32-fc52-41b6-bfe6-f18428c7bea8"],
 ", which on inputs of at most two photons is the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e6e0b96-e7ad-454e-a719-0fc0bcfec0ab"],
 " matrix sending ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{"0"},
     "Ket"], ",", 
    TemplateBox[{"1"},
     "Ket"], ",", 
    TemplateBox[{"2"},
     "Ket"]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d95eceef-fb6d-41f3-9b8e-5b5a69a6d76d"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{"0"},
     "Ket"], ",", 
    TemplateBox[{"1"},
     "Ket"]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fb899e29-4f34-4451-bf29-8854e5bd252c"],
 ". This ",
 ButtonBox["photon subtraction",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://www.science.org/doi/abs/10.1126/science.1146204"], None}],
 " is heralded, conditional on detecting the removed photon, so the map does \
not preserve the norm: it is the unnormalized operator applied to the state \
and renormalized after the herald."
}], "Text",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"c3d3bfe0-0447-4f44-8c8f-89cd300ce49f"],

Cell["\<\
For each kind of object, three things: its ordinary quantum meaning, what QF \
stores, and how QF uses what it stores.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"73a00beb-30eb-4a73-b992-2b1626e67741"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["state",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is a ket ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "28a36c5f-2f2e-4d21-8ac7-402e1cc267bf"],
 " or a density operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f0887e7-0bff-4692-b349-3e787aa7730b"],
 ", and an ",
 StyleBox["operator",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11a4f14d-1bc1-46a3-8aaf-91ed3a8041f5"],
 " is a linear map. An operator acts in three ways:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"3daa11ba-13bc-4cbf-b559-908be1b1405e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"], "\[Function]", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     TemplateBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
      "Ket"]}]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[Function]", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[Function]", 
    RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalE]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"289ac760-b4ef-46f9-97d7-591fe268b415"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15392e93-66e0-4645-aac5-2da75f1b5ea6"],
 " is an operator on kets; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f074fca-2cfd-43e1-b1f6-b12df52dafee"],
 " is the same operator acting on a density matrix by conjugation; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalE]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3df3ca74-f9fc-4d2d-b393-3866476336d2"],
 " is a general linear map on density matrices, which need not be a single \
conjugation, such as a channel or the generator of an open-system evolution. \
QF represents all three with ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7721c4bd-075a-49ef-adba-fd51d5bea5c5"],
 ": ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2ff4380b-12a5-46a2-85a7-bc9e5a22e8f1"],
 " by its matrix on kets, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e8a41ad0-3afa-4db0-9285-4a43a108af37"],
 " by that matrix acting through conjugation, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalE]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e8b9584e-8bac-4566-bfa4-cdb5ae70260c"],
 " by a matrix on the operator space."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"8ac13a1e-0ab3-4fe3-8714-d6643e49d254"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Mathematically a density operator is an operator, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "\[GreaterEqual]", "0"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2780b499-dfa6-4965-bcd8-fac12b888ea4"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1be20299-8232-4adb-a8eb-e9ac34329434"],
 "; the two differ in how QF stores them. QF stores a ket as its amplitudes \
with no input subsystem. It stores an ordinary operator by flattening its \
matrix into a single coefficient vector over the output and input subsystems \
together. It stores a density operator as a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumState"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c015fc0-8728-4046-a379-b75440860cab"],
 " carrying matrix coefficients, a ket index and its conjugate, with no input \
subsystem."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"a1adbc34-871c-4bc0-a170-df2a1b0e2c2b"],

Cell["\<\
So the storage records two independent things: whether the coefficients are a \
flattened vector or a matrix, and how the subsystems split into output and \
input. A density operator and an operator are the same kind of mathematical \
object stored two different ways; conflating the storage with the object, or \
calling both \"a vector,\" hides the split QF actually tracks.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->17830494,ExpressionUUID->"c702f4b2-2a57-42de-a65c-4abefe1decf3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["channel",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " and a ",
 StyleBox["measurement",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " are operators with one extra output subsystem set aside, and a ",
 StyleBox["circuit",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is a list of these placed on shared wires. The public objects and their \
meanings:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1589986527,ExpressionUUID->"2dbef215-6b25-40ae-985d-6fcf6ed49fa7"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["Object", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"530dc7f1-5e4e-46c9-b608-03816dea8ccc"],
     Cell["Quantum meaning", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"d4605e4d-06db-4228-9bc6-5804fe55b5a7"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData["QuantumState"], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "61a3f211-2d0f-4382-9834-4c9495302133"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "13985353-3f2d-42fb-9da0-87801cc7ad4e"], Cell[
    "a ket, or a density operator", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "b1d3a472-27c2-44e2-b598-927af74038b5"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData["QuantumOperator"], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "d4e4ac0e-9533-4940-b917-107479bcf316"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "29dd0057-8bf1-417d-bc68-4e75be99fe5f"], Cell[
    "a linear map, with an output side and an input side", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"93f6c992-4e7c-4a59-9585-880a218e1ecd"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData["QuantumChannel"], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "cfbd5a3b-c5d5-49dd-ab52-76a3bafcb929"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "ba3505a3-8b0c-431e-a041-09e7b7bd31a1"], Cell["\<\
a completely positive map, stored as a dilation with an environment set aside\
\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"31e08602-32cd-4cae-b21e-76c13b00600c"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    "QuantumMeasurementOperator"], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "e9e19184-b31a-4018-b736-063e6f00fa48"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "2a2c0598-4a6c-411f-81bb-75ef7fec9b59"], Cell["\<\
a general measurement, stored as a dilation with the outcome index kept \
rather than traced\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"2ccb46b9-eb0c-41e2-92e8-3ccbba897e98"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData["QuantumMeasurement"], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "c81697cb-050f-4ae1-8f6d-cfa51a59643c"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6e5708d8-ce99-4214-b5ae-05c278f3b489"], Cell["\<\
the result of a measurement: outcome probabilities and post-measurement states\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"0dcd5c91-38e4-4fdf-9c49-97e48692c958"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData["QuantumCircuitOperator"], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "a0ab2213-cd27-4465-8cbf-f132a779bf9f"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "ad76fc50-adbb-4377-a352-6a56a11668a4"], Cell[
    "a list of the above on numbered wires, a diagram", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"66bd8e8a-f54c-4949-8da7-6b564a8f640e"]}
  },
  GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
  GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
  GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {
      Scaled[0.44], 
      Scaled[0.44]}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
  GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.5}}, "Rows" -> {{0.8}}}]], "Text",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"b301367c-be06-45eb-8835-62c5dc6e3b9b"],

Cell["\<\
These heads are layers, each adding one thing to the one it contains:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"604e48b6-60ab-4335-b4fb-1fb6987f0fd6"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["Layer", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"ea23d3ee-3a31-4a45-bf76-baf448ef1f48"],
     Cell["What it contributes", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"8cdb6fa3-3249-4f86-a3fb-337546be8d57"]},
   {Cell[TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData["QuditBasis"], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "a4ab64e2-71f2-4093-bafd-f2df22bb8d3f"],
     ", ",
     Cell[BoxData["QuantumBasis"], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "66135ec0-e858-4996-94d5-59ae10595744"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"a7bc1f4e-b186-4e4c-ba0f-3e301122a5a0"], 
    Cell["\<\
the basis elements and subsystem dimensions on an output side and an input \
side, together with the picture and the parameters: everything needed to read \
an array as a state or an operator\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"dc916bf8-e8d4-4845-99d7-b867df0fd804"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData["QuantumState"], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "87d86e53-2635-452a-90f8-429f1fb67530"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "e7cf682f-816c-43f9-8a1f-cc31181467ed"], Cell[
    "a coefficient array together with that basis", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"b3e565ad-fe74-4c50-9a4c-9589931de548"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData["QuantumOperator"], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "3afccf5e-3bf9-47a6-8f11-1beae09a88ed"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "f69923a3-b95f-4e7b-b6ad-efef6c3586dc"], Cell[TextData[{
     "a ",
     Cell[BoxData["QuantumState"], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "c1ddd644-c592-4e65-a54a-e553cc34f7a4"],
     " placed on specified output and input wires"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"0c0f2191-95e0-45e9-a5e9-763ca760f3ba"]},
   {Cell[TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData["QuantumChannel"], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "9cd6365a-e819-4569-8883-c16fd8916386"],
     ", ",
     Cell[BoxData["QuantumMeasurementOperator"], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "39593526-df05-4940-b3b7-7fd63688da2e"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"8fcb51d4-a84d-43e9-86fd-1e384b149b68"], 
    Cell["\<\
an operator with one extra output wire, read as an environment or as an \
outcome\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"a309bdc1-1599-4664-8f50-0f6447febb11"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData["QuantumCircuitOperator"], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "7d1b830e-bf71-40b9-956c-27ccd7181a6f"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "8c155a12-76bf-4be8-a72b-62e524e8430a"], Cell["\<\
operations and their wiring, from which a method computes a result\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"d9659496-de1e-4b93-8db0-d45c27530513"]}
  },
  GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
  GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
  GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {
      Scaled[0.44], 
      Scaled[0.44]}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
  GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.5}}, "Rows" -> {{0.8}}}]], "Text",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"db86562d-b58c-4408-95a9-493e92cd11ff"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The exhaustive nesting is in Appendix A. A head names a representation, not \
a physical object. A ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumState"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e9f96a26-3576-4e0c-a9e7-7f2095b197b8"],
 " need only have the right shape; it need not be normalized or positive, and \
the same head holds the trace-zero output of a Liouvillian as readily as a \
physical state. Whether an object is a valid state, a unitary, or a \
trace-preserving channel is a separate question the constructor does not \
ask."
}], "Text",
 CellID->876231958,ExpressionUUID->"ac06ee91-fa93-40e4-a08b-ab9b3b545857"],

Cell["\<\
Throughout what follows the running example is one operator on a qubit on \
wire 1, introduced next.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1020575516,ExpressionUUID->"a4d627be-feef-454b-9800-940515498386"],

Cell["\<\
2. Coefficients and basis: stored numbers versus the represented map\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1967685850,ExpressionUUID->"42dee198-82b1-40f9-99f1-4d558565dc90"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The coefficients QF stores represent an operator in whatever basis is \
declared; the stored matrix can differ from the operator's matrix in the \
computational basis. Write ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["C", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fe4de8d-1e3a-4165-b3be-65c6e1f324b8"],
 " for the stored coefficient matrix and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "112cde6f-c78f-4f33-96d5-aaa0dc24cd89"],
 " for the same operator's computational-basis matrix. If the columns of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["out",
    FontSlant->"Plain"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c0f08fc1-4035-49fb-a70f-a3b9aa1fd67f"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["in",
    FontSlant->"Plain"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ed25e952-725e-4ee9-a25e-d7a842e50dc5"],
 " are the declared output and input basis vectors, then"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1044562475,ExpressionUUID->"fdf04b78-a569-4dac-9942-ee0e3877c22e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "=", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["out",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["C", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["in",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1653200050,ExpressionUUID->"ede81200-d461-4fc1-9039-4428f8790653"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This needs only that the basis matrices ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["out",
    FontSlant->"Plain"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b0d6b396-f47c-4158-b0c6-b609567fbcaa"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["in",
    FontSlant->"Plain"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ad5cb14-2919-47e6-8885-b74eda6749a2"],
 " are invertible; it does not need them orthonormal. A concrete case: store ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "92b37d49-353e-478f-9db5-d5c5eee3c868"],
 " and declare the basis to be the eigenbasis of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "de68351f-fde1-425f-aa94-73e94f70d038"],
 ", with columns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"+"},
    "Ket"], ",", 
   TemplateBox[{"-"},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "156afa34-ec67-404f-85e5-4f639eb061e0"],
 ". Then ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      TemplateBox[{"+"},
       "Ket"], 
      TemplateBox[{"+"},
       "Bra"]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{
      TemplateBox[{"-"},
       "Ket"], 
      TemplateBox[{"-"},
       "Bra"]}]}], "=", 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e3931fe0-3684-4882-ae03-c9c5125eac35"],
 ": the stored coefficients ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1eb58fdc-4286-4cc9-8f5c-ebc0ab288108"],
 " represent the operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0892d636-43b2-4ad8-9224-c9fa2c3c9f49"],
 " in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f0a303d-f7e1-4c14-906c-6a77fce53ef0"],
 " basis, though the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["C", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f4431e4d-4652-4a94-8b1e-e170a517ddc8"],
 " in the computational basis would be ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "17b1925f-6fd1-4c68-a7a0-a6c5fe362239"],
 ". In QF this is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["R", "TI"], "="}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65adb349-05d5-460d-93ea-581e1c1d33d9"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "\"\<PauliX\>\""}], 
   "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c0c53232-54d2-42c7-b499-abaaac0482a7"],
 "; its stored coefficient matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["C", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cf4e30ab-7412-4454-acc6-a7da749b4890"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fb39b9d0-4738-494c-aec5-0503163791a5"],
 " and its computational matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79ceffc8-ed19-4f73-af0b-0e83f2b71eec"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d6f0783-7243-4358-aade-29472fb03c49"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f4177f8-8eac-4ec6-a201-0becc355d3aa"],
 " is the running operator."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1384978530,ExpressionUUID->"acc551bf-8089-4b7c-b66c-fa33a7fb3e18"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two constructions use the basis for opposite purposes, and QF keeps them \
apart. Declaring a basis fixes what supplied numbers mean: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "\"\<PauliX\>\""}], 
   "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "015d3c27-3fb1-4e2b-8c78-c32dd533cd16"],
 " reads the numbers ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72f8c35a-6d36-4266-a8ed-0e009f3d84cd"],
 " as coefficients in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4773396b-1daa-4890-a123-962336405aaf"],
 " basis, and so builds ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47607c3d-8dbf-4144-a7b8-54f0c70dbf09"],
 ". Converting an existing object to another basis preserves the object and \
recomputes its numbers: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
    " ", "\"\<PauliX\>\""}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bad581cb-aa15-456f-b805-36fa13f96c35"],
 " takes the operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6a10640f-42c0-409c-acce-bc6590488e00"],
 ", already built, and re-expresses it in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "066194b7-2ce2-41d9-bfbc-4b6966c4553f"],
 " basis, where its stored matrix becomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6c9959fc-de94-4476-b4ba-026a6734e889"],
 ". The first turns numbers into an operator; the second turns an operator \
into different numbers for the same operator. Both reach ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d65a5a8a-84a9-4951-8924-6cd6b02b1bc2"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->519689844,ExpressionUUID->"b8bf5047-372b-47af-a1e0-611cd169042a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A change of coordinates preserves the operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b4a27de5-57a2-43ba-aedf-760bed38b297"],
 "; applying a gate changes the state. This is why QF reconciles bases before \
it composes: coefficients on a shared subsystem cannot be contracted until \
both sides are written in one basis. The ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumBasis"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e7f2511c-5009-4af0-a2a7-77eb92154350"],
 " also records a picture, the convention that fixes how the stored \
coefficients are read. This account treats the Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger, \
Heisenberg, and phase-space pictures; the kernel also stores an interaction \
picture, which is outside this account."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1609367578,ExpressionUUID->"e65c3bec-5cfa-43fc-ad66-8cf516ad2c69"],

Cell["3. Maps on density matrices", "Section",
 CellID->1541450781,ExpressionUUID->"111727e6-59f4-40db-9470-f7feb0383547"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The map ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[Function]", "\[ScriptCapitalE]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "081b9e37-d20b-47b7-811e-49f1cbb3d804"],
 " on density matrices is the foundation for channels, evolution, and the \
phase-space picture. It cannot always be written as a single conjugation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[Function]", 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b5f08ae8-1028-49cd-bb1b-e1e0d6d1b91f"],
 ": a channel is a sum ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f5a844c-b451-4209-b3ba-7954afcb9d3f"],
 ", and the generator of a continuous evolution is a commutator plus \
dissipators. QF represents such a map the same way it represents an operator, \
as a matrix of coefficients. The step that makes this possible is to turn ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d2ca4508-8692-4839-8fa9-d44c963dc9fd"],
 " into a vector."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1657269721,ExpressionUUID->"b451b15a-c5db-4a84-83ad-df8ef91638ee"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a system of dimension ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f98f3ae-d1e6-497a-bfe8-66006d4da30a"],
 ", vectorization arranges the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d9387d12-9807-4c95-9fd8-22469c259d99"],
 " elements of its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "\[Times]", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "241c526f-3c48-470b-9a1c-5acc6834d3b6"],
 " density matrix into a vector of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f7608e7-815e-4b95-b3a2-65dfe265a7e4"],
 ", and a map on density matrices then becomes a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], "2"], "\[Times]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "386ebf2c-34b2-48f1-97b0-967cda0fc8d1"],
 " matrix acting on that vector. That matrix is again a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "91256437-2832-4ad4-a95e-12070dd9103a"],
 ", on the operator space of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "\[Times]", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8fc245d4-9624-4570-b6ff-3bc2d05b0ff1"],
 " matrices. It is how the map is represented; applying the map need not \
build it in full, since a tensor contraction can carry out the same action. \
Left and right multiplication are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Left\>\"", "[", "A", "]"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ab07dde8-d69b-4945-84a1-02ea2ccc9edb"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"=", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
    StyleBox["I", "TI"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4234335c-0afd-40f0-a13c-a08d7eafb7c1"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Right\>\"", "[", "A", "]"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "310bde5a-b2da-44cd-a2bc-e80103b8ffe1"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"=", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T",
      FontFamily->"Helvetica",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "135eadf3-4f7f-4220-a2ff-7056e5890f56"],
 "; a conjugation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[Function]", 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e9e005c2-b531-4172-99b5-08b36595c11d"],
 " combines left multiplication by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d9a3beb5-e31a-47cb-95b1-9323f9fe572a"],
 " with right multiplication by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a42b8ffd-4480-4dc4-942a-f22bb96b4807"],
 "; the generator of the von Neumann equation is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Liouvillian\>\"", "[", "H", "]"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54bd09ab-ccac-49e5-b8d3-bfdddae26b1a"],
 ", the matrix of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], ",", "\[CenterDot]"}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41892c6f-2340-4597-97c3-bd390a4416f6"],
 ". The Liouvillian of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f4234f47-c722-4a8c-8694-2007ad464f57"],
 " applied to the density matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"0"},
    "Ket"], 
   TemplateBox[{"0"},
    "Bra"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10781922-758d-46cc-9a3d-6ed61a359b29"],
 " returns the commutator, a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumState"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ef4413d0-099f-4562-bf45-dde8eba35902"],
 " of trace zero:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1140508347,ExpressionUUID->"b73ca98b-f709-4cd0-89f0-ba841ea47b10"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", 
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{"\<\"Liouvillian\"\>", 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["[",
         SpanMaxSize->1], "\<\"X\"\>", 
        StyleBox["]",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}],
     FontFamily->"Courier",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{"0"},
      "Ket"], 
     TemplateBox[{"0"},
      "Bra"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], "[", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
       RowBox[{
        TemplateBox[{"0"},
         "Ket"], 
        TemplateBox[{"0"},
         "Bra"]}]}], "]"}]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
        {"0", 
         StyleBox["i", "TI"]},
        {
         RowBox[{"-", 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]}], "0"}
       }], ")"}], "."}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->496109794,ExpressionUUID->"bc5b1d00-c0aa-4248-bb79-c081b0d6baf5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The stored coefficients and this matrix are the same numbers read with \
different indices. To build the matrix that acts on the vectorized density \
operator, QF reshapes the stored coefficient array and swaps its two index \
groups (the property ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<StateMatrix\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e9e67494-a75c-4d96-9fff-088acaa3ca15"],
 "); the numbers do not change, only their arrangement. Two steps are worth \
separating: ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Bend\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2fb4b643-25ad-482a-9c5c-6d3966eaa16c"],
 " forms the density matrix, from a ket as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"], 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Bra"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6524e5fe-81b1-4cc1-8c2f-929512976c72"],
 " and from a stored matrix as itself, then vectorizes it into the ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<DensityVector\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ceac0db-2e67-4de4-855f-866f3a7b1e0a"],
 " of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ba0779ee-20f2-4433-b3fa-e57a004b130a"],
 "; ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Double\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c1015ff-0fc0-4001-98f6-d5b3a6eff4f5"],
 " additionally interleaves the axes so each subsystem sits beside its \
conjugate, the arrangement the maps above act on."
}], "Text",
 CellID->108435171,ExpressionUUID->"8880a569-8322-4beb-9f03-579539f8c2cd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Three things now share one model. A channel is the map ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[Function]", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "afa7ab15-1703-4dd8-a7be-4b4d31cd1a3a"],
 ", an operator-space matrix that QF stores as a dilation with an environment \
rather than as the matrix itself. A continuous evolution integrates the map \
generated by the Liouvillian, or by the Lindbladian when there are \
dissipators. The phase-space picture is a change of coordinates of this same \
matrix. Each is the same operator-space representation read or generated \
differently, not a separate mechanism."
}], "Text",
 CellID->829388421,ExpressionUUID->"242f6f98-bc46-4569-a2a8-b706f18d9170"],

Cell["4. Combining objects", "Section",
 CellID->203008389,ExpressionUUID->"7a5a9e83-94f1-4939-bad0-9c41bf8269f9"],

Cell["\<\
Apply, compose, tensor, adjoint, and discard, each with what QF does to \
perform it.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1090263105,ExpressionUUID->"abf002b1-9638-4997-98d3-472f5ea5db4d"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["Operation", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"b92422ff-0027-4ec2-b007-6efe0a4195d0"],
     Cell["Meaning", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"440c93a6-52f7-4414-ba4c-b9e0388ac126"],
     Cell["What QF adds", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"6746b367-80c4-4ae6-939d-ac45ce4acfa9"]},
   {Cell["Apply to a ket", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "5b9b45a7-30b0-4cae-a370-32d655030c02"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
       "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "f5a1cdb3-e77d-44f5-8023-526ebd88bd5e"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "2776b7cf-60dd-4028-a752-0c607bd48d1a"], Cell["\<\
reads the state on the input wires, carries untouched wires unchanged, \
reconciles the basis\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"8b601715-cf13-4fd5-9b8e-e7cc256696b4"]},
   {Cell["Apply to a density matrix", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "b6cefeb3-d24c-4abb-9977-fca6a43568a3"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "1d7071d5-0465-493c-8cd9-a3d23b24eb46"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "9a39a568-2546-4691-b614-0039d45a16e1"], Cell[
    "the same, on the stored density coefficients", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"38cd7d8d-2f3b-4b6a-96cd-ee9a8d0e4356"]},
   {Cell[TextData[{
     "Compose (",
     Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "2f586442-e7fc-418d-be3e-e21d3dbb65f8"],
     " then ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "263ff5cf-0747-42ff-8b1c-fb1276e1da41"],
     ")"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"66b09634-146b-4e6d-8c2b-3057054a1d93"], 
    Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"A", "B"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "1b69d84e-3c7a-4803-a7e6-3d373e0fa202"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "97ec8634-a147-468f-934e-d1b1311939e0"], Cell[
    "contracts the shared wire, aligning bases first", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"59c7ae51-e2f5-4c0a-b3dd-66fdd7cfde53"]},
   {Cell["Tensor", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "b2fdc1df-79d9-4266-adca-f8eb7bdfe41f"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
      StyleBox["B", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "caafe378-f741-4f1c-b613-818b2d908367"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "53750381-761a-4103-b2cd-7cb69607169d"], Cell[
    "places on disjoint wires, renumbering to avoid clashes", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"c57e82d5-a9be-4b99-97d7-72232f80ba6e"]},
   {Cell["Adjoint", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "5befe7a3-28ea-40a6-9df7-a61889c1cfd6"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "aaebf00b-12b1-489e-8e69-ec637f5ec0d1"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "99ee4a22-65cd-4589-8945-0a326daa63cb"], Cell["\<\
swaps input and output and conjugates; the physical adjoint only on \
orthonormal bases\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"16bc7fbc-b13a-48a2-b137-bb5347e40df7"]},
   {Cell["Discard a subsystem", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "286d6fdd-d2cf-453d-a759-15578642d606"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["Tr",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "64c9bc25-161e-4017-af37-d3b35e4d3047"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "d9c04fce-ecf6-4ba0-a779-7b82f9aef794"], Cell[
    "contracts the discarded subsystem's row and column indices", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"ae5a7d46-9489-4cc5-9f9f-fe52581bfeb9"]}
  },
  GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
  GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
  GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {
      Scaled[0.3], 
      Scaled[0.1], 
      Scaled[0.5]}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
  GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.5}}, "Rows" -> {{0.8}}}]], "Text",
 CellID->1560876240,ExpressionUUID->"9442591b-b5f4-4b66-9b89-70f0a551481d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Applying.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " An operator acts on the wires it names and leaves the rest alone. Pauli ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8ea82500-a766-492a-9312-1b1ee67c4540"],
 " on qubit 1 of a two-qubit register sends ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"00"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5a820f68-39e0-4ccf-aeb5-6be70c8f5d7d"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"10"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "317b670f-9f95-4646-9641-b68a38157f11"],
 ": QF puts an identity on qubit 2 and matches the dimension on qubit 1. If \
the state has fewer qubits than the operator reaches, QF pads it with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65425b5b-b48f-4b85-a361-7a3386d803b5"],
 " on the missing wires. On a density matrix the same operator gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a6231f46-e1cf-4277-9ca9-efe4d887c70a"],
 ". The result carries a basis of its own, so its stored amplitudes need not \
be its computational amplitudes; applying ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ebc32e97-4c67-4a00-8782-9cad5af986c1"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "571c22b9-38b5-4c37-934e-cbd1bfae6e25"],
 " gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d665df66-ee41-4c0f-a46b-2955765d60c3"],
 ", stored as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66ae52df-2762-486b-9dc3-1ed9d7d30df0"],
 " in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8c86577d-0567-449a-b059-9aafd6bd6abc"],
 " basis."
}], "Text",
 CellID->176337227,ExpressionUUID->"62b2b129-2562-4a28-93ab-6272ff568551"],

Cell["\<\
Applying runs as a short sequence, and the other operations share its shape. \
QF reads which wires the operator and the state have in common and their \
dimensions; writes both on a common basis, changing coordinates when the \
shared wires carry different ones; takes the amplitude form for a ket and the \
vectorized form for a density matrix; contracts the shared wires; and \
rebuilds the result as a new object carrying its own basis and wire orders. \
Compose, tensor, and trace are the same steps with a different contraction, \
and a method runs this for a whole circuit at once.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->807053435,ExpressionUUID->"c1b7935f-57dd-497b-b97a-d8e64ab89b82"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Composing.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Applying ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35cd2a51-2268-4cbd-bcd9-0a30a8f4dacd"],
 " then ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "22905977-65b0-49df-9f94-26d25f1d49e7"],
 " is the matrix product ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"A", "B"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c06aa8f8-0a47-4e37-9025-5c5abc02dd64"],
 ","
}], "Text",
 CellID->1633675818,ExpressionUUID->"7d1e340d-0d4d-4a3d-80fa-29902ee08efa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      StyleBox[
       RowBox[{"A", "B"}], "TI"], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"i", "k"}], "TI"]], "=", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1828793009,ExpressionUUID->"e2f750dd-e3c6-4b91-ad0b-f02d02be1765"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The summed index ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "de8737db-7f96-43cc-8c35-d1eea6d6ea7e"],
 " runs over the basis of the shared subsystem, the one ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2ef5f5da-f8ae-4c26-8e77-ae1df25ae2cd"],
 " takes as input and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c10dcb60-fda0-4cc3-a936-38dcf8e7c531"],
 " produces as output. QF contracts that subsystem, keeps every subsystem the \
contraction does not touch (the remaining outputs and inputs of both \
operands), and on the shared subsystem writes both operators in one basis \
before summing. When the two operators overlap only partially, this is the \
general rule: composing a two-qubit gate on wires 1 and 2 with a one-qubit \
gate on wire 2 contracts wire 2 and leaves wire 1's output and the two-qubit \
gate's other input in place. Maps on density matrices compose by the same \
contraction on the operator space, so a channel after a channel, or a gate \
after a channel, is one more contraction."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1232986364,ExpressionUUID->"0ceced26-c386-47d2-9396-37365e449aa4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That basis step is where the stored coefficients matter. Compose ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "709214c0-26a2-4f45-8662-1e15cf1e014d"],
 " after ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79d3aba4-e75f-4ab5-b5fe-6fac87fa0258"],
 ", whose stored coefficient matrix is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ccda0024-dce7-444d-8a80-516b74325172"],
 " although the operator is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d40bf1e-6e8f-403e-bf65-6299e2ca8f27"],
 ". Contracting the stored numbers as they sit would give ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1059d861-8cae-4e86-85f5-1e17692dcfa9"],
 ", the wrong operator. QF reconciles the bases and returns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Z", "X"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9bfd0f0a-77c3-43fd-92fa-1f8a39e2d150"],
 ","
}], "Text",
 CellID->762269937,ExpressionUUID->"7a8dbc07-f0ba-4639-ba11-2ceeb7886488"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "=", "(", GridBox[{
      {"0", "1"},
      {
       RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "0"}
     }], ")"}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->405213039,ExpressionUUID->"121e8cab-668c-4578-a5ed-c451a05dadf8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Adjoint.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dad0259-b2db-4925-8631-c67c4ca6e19d"],
 " swaps the input and output sides and conjugate-transposes the \
coefficients. This is the physical adjoint only when the bases are \
orthonormal. In general, with Gram matrices ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["G", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["F", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   StyleBox["F", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49788b55-f5c6-4b62-b63f-ddda87842acd"],
 " on each side, the adjoint of the represented map has coefficients ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["in",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["C", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["out",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "38087f86-3dde-43a4-b926-91c57baced14"],
 ", and QF omits the Gram factors, so on a non-orthonormal basis one first \
changes to the computational basis."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2118931930,ExpressionUUID->"b0a299d2-a55c-48f1-bea1-7ed876b221f6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Tensor product.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
   StyleBox["B", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a49add9-0daa-4ae1-a929-bd1f2b914473"],
 " places the two operators on disjoint wires, renumbering ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e354bde0-52b0-423b-8d75-24f94a639734"],
 "'s wires so none clashes; the pictures are not checked for compatibility, \
and the first operand's picture is adopted."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1039057480,ExpressionUUID->"c1f6d5f5-72c7-4dc6-a94c-e40073f86173"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Discarding.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The partial trace has one rule per object. On a density matrix, discarding \
a subsystem sums over the matching row and column indices of that subsystem, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Tr",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "afbf0515-7fff-4f80-9904-4cd25f83db5b"],
 ". On an operator, a trace pair contracts one output wire against one input \
wire; the two wires must carry the same basis, or the result is the trace of \
the stored coefficients rather than the trace of the map. On a circuit, the \
trace is drawn as a cap: a wire that closes the two ends into a loop."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1411198270,ExpressionUUID->"f728d1c6-977d-4ace-9c03-7eeda6c581d9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Circuits.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A circuit is the composition of its listed operations on numbered wires, \
applied in order. QF composes them by the same contraction, so the circuit is \
one object; a method turns the diagram into a value."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1703453532,ExpressionUUID->"3b7afd79-b891-4105-b90d-ba720f4d03ed"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The correctness requirement for composition.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Convert the composed object to its computational matrix and you get the \
product of the two operators' computational matrices, once both are placed on \
a common register with identities on the untouched subsystems and their bases \
are aligned. This holds for any invertible basis matrices on the shared \
subsystems, and it rests entirely on the change-of-basis step."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1477609488,ExpressionUUID->"10b17f37-523a-4645-8868-8cb7acb82959"],

Cell["\<\
Composition needs the shared subsystems to carry the same dimensions. A \
dimension mismatch is refused. A mismatch between the Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger \
and Heisenberg pictures is not refused; it is silently resolved to the Schr\
\[ODoubleDot]dinger picture. A phase-space operand instead fails on a \
dimension mismatch.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1030824397,ExpressionUUID->"b14f8880-245c-4d9b-a72e-d8cb1b25a632"],

Cell["5. Channels and measurements", "Section",
 CellID->100031176,ExpressionUUID->"746f0264-b4c7-45c1-95c0-8f7e9feaaf4d"],

Cell["\<\
A channel and a measurement both come from a family of operators, but the \
family means different things and the list constructors read it differently. \
That difference fixes the physical object the user creates.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->144223354,ExpressionUUID->"d29b3ef7-0068-441f-bd15-d8e9fe1e2485"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["channel",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is the map ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[Function]", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07c0455f-9c16-49c3-92d0-fea0dffe9b65"],
 ", the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "637ac333-fcc4-4d8c-828b-71f7979d0627"],
 " its Kraus operators. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumChannel", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"M1", ",", " ", "M2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d8e874ea-efb3-46ed-a3c3-a64e744a6356"],
 " reads the list as Kraus operators directly. QF stores the family as one \
operator with an extra output subsystem,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1443527617,ExpressionUUID->"62c2bf53-f4f7-4ea5-8b97-a5e09519c163"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"],
      LimitsPositioning->False], 
     RowBox[{
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["m", "TI"]},
       "Ket"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->311511756,ExpressionUUID->"736f0682-f03f-4178-9c36-74ef4fad596d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "the Kraus operators stacked along that index; discarding the index, the \
environment, and tracing it out returns the map. This is the Stinespring \
form: a dilation followed by a trace. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ed79de6a-7627-498d-8c93-a06b974dc183"],
 " is an isometry, and the map preserves the trace, exactly when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d2b74a0e-36a7-447a-b2d1-e47ef11726b3"],
 ", which QF does not check at construction and exposes as ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<TracePreservingQ\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d00684a-31a4-4d73-8722-b74a075b007d"],
 "; a channel built from an arbitrary list is completely positive but need \
not preserve the trace. On the running qubit, the bit-flip channel ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumChannel", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
       RowBox[{"3", "/", "4"}], "]"}], " ", "I"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}], "]"}], " ", "X"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c8532eb-61d7-4792-80f1-10a89382ad96"],
 " sends ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"0"},
    "Ket"], 
   TemplateBox[{"0"},
    "Bra"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "153c2512-468a-4c84-a3b0-0bbc1c4ec4e6"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"3", "/", "4"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1bb688df-daf4-486a-a380-33a165c2070b"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1381425643,ExpressionUUID->"3c2c100d-56c9-42e2-9f14-d4176050d697"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["measurement",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is read branch by branch. With measurement operators ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d231c40-7382-466f-9940-11b138798b15"],
 " acting on a state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f66575b4-fecc-4fc3-9b23-16041fade3dc"],
 " by"
}], "Text",
 CellID->377280352,ExpressionUUID->"af167b6f-9bb3-448f-9eb3-39697c4e6dbe"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalI]", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["Tr",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     SubscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalI]", 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalI]", 
        StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], " ", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["m", "TI"]], ">", "0"}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1717363484,ExpressionUUID->"3b837036-96c3-48fc-92b5-63280449a7ce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "four things are distinct and QF keeps them distinct: the unnormalized \
branch ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalI]", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3ee3a09f-bfb3-4656-a796-e32ec3bfa2f9"],
 ", its probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f19088fa-ea7c-4139-bea3-4a7a1b5199c0"],
 ", the conditional state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "96540cdf-dda8-48a3-92fe-0301d2ada0d8"],
 ", and the state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalI]", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fec612f0-2b32-4a7c-b68c-524b159ed762"],
 " obtained by ignoring the outcome. The probabilities alone come from the \
effects ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c969ccbc-1720-481b-8c79-b5d7fba6aa17"],
 ", a positive operator-valued measure (POVM), through the Born rule ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30e9bbbd-9402-415e-8d64-c08a84945971"],
 "; the POVM fixes the probabilities but not the disturbance, since many \
measurement operators share one effect."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1781880651,ExpressionUUID->"ba4f843e-a382-4ca3-bf5b-a01a40900bfb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The list constructors read a measurement's family as effects, not as Kraus \
operators. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumMeasurementOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"E1", ",", " ", "E2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f1803c2d-c1a0-4258-9e84-7879dfaf80a4"],
 " takes the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71c9b96d-6ec1-4940-91d4-486c2aa11912"],
 " to be POVM effects and forms each measurement operator as the matrix \
square root ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8e2dbb2a-0d23-40ff-94a2-bab2b12fe0a7"],
 ", the canonical choice. The stored measurement operators are these ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e89e15e2-4cc6-45c9-bf42-f00dec58bb12"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<POVMElements\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "440028ba-602a-48dd-ba21-6ac0702f3085"],
 " returns the effects, rescaled so their sum has unit mean diagonal; it \
returns them verbatim only when the supplied effects already sum that way. An \
observable is its own construction: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumMeasurementOperator", "[", "obs", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d613b1ca-113f-4844-832e-dcb1df7abe4e"],
 " measures a Hermitian operator in its eigenbasis. So the same list of \
matrices builds a different object under ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumChannel"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dee5bcc2-a79c-4217-a5db-8aea0b150529"],
 ", where it is Kraus operators, than under ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumMeasurementOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "28a0dd42-36c7-4904-a060-b12b9af3725e"],
 ", where it is effects."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1536527082,ExpressionUUID->"8d2dbef9-b193-49c6-a8a2-8fff6bb13e4f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The measurement stores its family as the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{
       StyleBox["m", "TI"]},
      "Ket"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d1b53027-e0ba-490f-98df-5461bea9e53c"],
 ", now with the extra index kept to carry the outcome. This is where the \
QF-specific semantics lives: the extra index can be kept as a live wire, a \
bare isometry with nothing measured yet; discarded, the channel above; or \
read, the measurement. Kept, the branches stay coherent in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fcacba5-e660-47f0-b482-e8de806490b2"],
 " and record no classical outcome; the outcome becomes classical only once \
the index is read."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1621535814,ExpressionUUID->"d1f24231-2d12-45a9-9f59-f6d006cf20a7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Read, applying the measurement returns a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumMeasurement"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b55144a-bff3-4d9d-8a67-237a72a4c997"],
 " exposing ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Probabilities\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b46bba71-13d4-4c97-9caf-93cad74aad9b"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<States\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d6485aa4-b6a6-4a28-b1db-429f83f89f43"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<PostMeasurementState\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f9ccacad-f498-4611-89db-905ac20f94bb"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Probabilities\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fe32530b-4d91-44f4-98e8-083c32621743"],
 " is the Born distribution, an association keyed by outcome; the bare vector \
is ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8fa3eb40-376d-43f3-a489-d9749555650b"],
 ", and returning either is not sampling a single outcome. ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<States\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c7126764-e5ff-4990-9e54-2737765d66ad"],
 " returns the branch states on the full register, not the normalized \
conditional states ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35ca500d-fed5-49aa-85f9-d986ed8a12bb"],
 ". For a pure input each branch comes back as the unnormalized ket ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "92981d5f-f76e-4a00-97e2-7c08d35b7a03"],
 ", of norm ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b048690-a320-47ac-aef1-fad953b17c23"],
 ". Its density operator is the branch ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalI]", 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Bra"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ecc4bf44-cf35-4545-8cc1-02cb6083ffed"],
 ", of trace ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c9f28170-a4eb-43a9-9974-8f40123e428a"],
 ". Measuring one qubit of a Bell state returns two branch kets of norm ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2fc2c2dd-ec16-4a19-a1fd-a84277525a78"],
 ", each the unnormalized half of the split with probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a5993f10-053f-465d-9ee8-bd4c2000ee0a"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<PostMeasurementState\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "428e3e0c-9bab-49fa-9ac2-5fe04fbd63ed"],
 " reduces to the target subsystems, tracing out the outcome index and every \
non-target subsystem, so it is not the full-register object ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<States\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "379d87ee-a686-4184-b959-471ff22efe33"],
 " returns."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1193935837,ExpressionUUID->"0da79b2e-a377-4e03-8d89-e9ee2a6c9713"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"R", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cd937e69-d0d3-4e7f-8db6-8f0435eda7d1"],
 " is the stored ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "752ee6d8-6c61-4201-8ee1-6af124406318"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"R", "[", "\"\<MatrixRepresentation\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29f4b70c-4320-469e-8103-67db08ba2f33"],
 " is its computational matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a6dff96-b21b-4671-8677-5dca5970c27d"],
 "; applying it, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"R", "[", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13e00814-be04-4e3c-ba44-db4fc462c402"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bcd945e9-ab26-4397-8e3b-c97ebbd88c0f"],
 ", stored ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "83817b2c-d989-4883-8039-a8ac2fb36618"],
 " in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d23ed7c5-6307-44bf-9c52-77f654f1544a"],
 " basis. Measuring the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c97095dd-20e5-4b71-87a0-df4691d8cce1"],
 " observable on that state, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"QuantumMeasurementOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
   RowBox[{"R", "[", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0973fe8a-fab3-4742-9810-4d37499c551b"],
 ", returns a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumMeasurement"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "350041a2-b3ed-4c23-b2b9-640edb60ae2c"],
 " with probabilities ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1", "/", "2"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", "2", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "488b10c4-341e-436a-8f68-b7cbe9249bf0"],
 " and two branch kets of norm ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9fe3052e-b069-4139-88b3-6da0ccec78e1"],
 ", the split of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"1"},
    "Ket"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      TemplateBox[{"+"},
       "Ket"], "-", 
      TemplateBox[{"-"},
       "Ket"]}], ")"}], "/", 
    SqrtBox["2"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b5eeb4e-f2e9-42af-8108-13f557126fe2"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->105329933,ExpressionUUID->"36ac53af-cbc9-4b1a-b6ab-e0aaf026078c"],

Cell["6. Parameters and evolution", "Section",
 CellID->1234416869,ExpressionUUID->"cf9d98af-04fb-4bd6-93de-d48cf710f03f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A parameterized operator is a family indexed by the values of its \
parameters, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "\[Function]", 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2ed51e0a-dad2-418d-8b85-1bc5dad95c00"],
 "; QF records the parameter names and their ranges alongside the \
coefficients, and composing two families composes them value by value on the \
union of their names. Substituting a parameter value is evaluation at a \
point, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "0"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "eb052905-e438-4468-97dd-753510064fcd"],
 ". Because the host is a computer-algebra system, an amplitude may itself \
stay symbolic, so a value can enter either as a declared parameter or as a \
symbolic amplitude; which one to use is a modeling choice."
}], "Text",
 CellID->240380995,ExpressionUUID->"1f4754f3-82c9-400f-bf42-901acd2c27af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Continuous-time evolution is ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumEvolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9b6dbe86-19a9-402d-a517-0dc6c3603ba3"],
 ", and it acts on the representations already built. From a Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["H", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ae084a17-7253-4ca5-bd25-2c37c34b6dea"],
 " it integrates the Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger equation on the state; from a \
Hamiltonian, a list of Lindblad operators, and rates it integrates the map \
generated by the Lindbladian, so the evolved object is a density-matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumState"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3884d024-5d22-419a-bee5-feb6a34d6d04"],
 ". With no initial state it returns the propagator as an operator, and from \
an initial observable it returns the Heisenberg-picture evolution as an \
operator. The equation is solved when ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumEvolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7103eb-4e58-4912-a80c-58f95a733671"],
 " is called, since the solver runs inside the constructor; only the \
evaluation of the stored solution at a chosen time is deferred. On the \
running qubit, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Z\>\"", "]"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    "\[Rho]", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d305c875-3213-424e-93eb-7f8cdc609234"],
 " returns a state whose density matrix carries the time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2896a819-5a8e-4fb4-a1b3-f1740c341ac4"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1771870337,ExpressionUUID->"40505f0c-b270-4d33-ba34-f545e963b466"],

Cell["7. Coordinate changes: phase space", "Section",
 CellID->305160771,ExpressionUUID->"5eca6664-6e90-41a7-8cb4-4a740ac6fe01"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A phase-space picture is a change of coordinates of the operator-space \
representation. Until now a basis has been the state vectors that expand a \
ket; here it is an operator basis, a set of matrices ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c4c9e909-ace5-4c79-804f-167ad00eca81"],
 " that expand a density matrix as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3ea9332d-c2e1-4ac2-9034-c27c063ea0ac"],
 ". For one qubit the four matrices ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c54cf789-d4a5-46aa-ac04-ad9fdf2eccf8"],
 " are such a basis. Which picture the ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumBasis"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fcb024a0-2e99-4b81-8c76-fbfdca929ef9"],
 " records fixes what the coefficients are: a ket's amplitudes, a density \
matrix's matrix elements in the Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger picture, and in a \
phase-space picture the operator-basis coefficients ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fe28d9a9-45e6-4a31-bbad-6efa0fcdd1b8"],
 ", which are quasi-probabilities; the Heisenberg picture instead carries the \
evolution on operators rather than states. QF reaches a phase-space picture \
with ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumPhaseSpaceTransform"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "323fdc4a-aba6-4a9f-b669-55c56892f717"],
 ": read the operator-space coefficients in an operator basis with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "87154897-fa73-4c8f-91ab-5ee69cb4e5ba"],
 " elements per subsystem. Because it is a change of coordinates of the \
operator-space matrices, it preserves composition and application: \
transforming a product gives the product of the transforms. When both the \
density matrix and the operator basis are Hermitian, as the Wigner, Pauli, \
and Gell-Mann bases are, the coefficients ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "acb0b6aa-336d-47fd-800d-521e1cb37777"],
 " are real, though the vectorized matrix is complex."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1896945989,ExpressionUUID->"6cc8b5b8-4652-4177-a801-958423041ace"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A complete operator basis always gives coordinates, its expansion \
coefficients fixing the density matrix; a measurement's outcome probabilities \
fix it only when the measurement is informationally complete, which an \
arbitrary POVM need not be. The Wigner basis (displaced parities in odd \
dimension, and a half-phase variant in even dimension) gives the discrete \
Wigner function; a Hermitian operator basis gives real Bloch-like components; \
an informationally complete POVM, such as the symmetric informationally \
complete (SIC) POVM of the named ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<QBismSIC\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "db191e28-ded2-4b32-a201-7f78c254b8a9"],
 " basis, gives its outcome probabilities as coordinates, built from the \
POVM's dual operators. The inverse, ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumWeylTransform"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b885243-a27a-45cb-a992-e8b1e8c2efd9"],
 ", takes square roots of the dimensions and returns to the \
Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger picture; it recovers a density matrix exactly but \
forgets the global phase of a ket or a unitary, because the density matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aa18e9b4-aa0a-48fd-a9b9-f69fb46808c3"],
 " does not carry it. The rate matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"HamiltonianTransitionRate", "[", "H", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e4c451c2-d861-41d4-a4b8-20da68a54e0f"],
 " is the Liouvillian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], ",", "\[CenterDot]"}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77b733bf-8021-428e-9ff9-0ca2dd0952bd"],
 " expressed directly in these coordinates. The even-dimension convention, \
the weighted trace-preservation condition, and the sign-sector transform are \
in Appendix C."
}], "Text",
 CellID->653417278,ExpressionUUID->"7fa7592d-800f-4959-8186-e1762e801e15"],

Cell["8. The stabilizer representation", "Section",
 CellID->1067269536,ExpressionUUID->"a5909573-4e2f-4078-bcd2-25e758b524f5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A qubit stabilizer state is a different data structure, a tableau: the \
group of Pauli operators that fixes the state, stored as bits, with one \
recorded global phase. It is not a tensor of amplitudes, and QF joins it to \
the tensor representation by two conversions. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "ps", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "93b09b82-7372-46c5-9e43-5a5fc75e5118"],
 " builds the state vector from the tableau and multiplies in the recorded \
global phase; its cost is set by the construction it uses, a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["2", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "\[Times]", 
   SuperscriptBox["2", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16a83184-f0a3-41b8-8a90-ba583bc5b966"],
 " operator and its null space, not by the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["2", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e7a6377-a12d-44ee-8e76-7160379eb655"],
 " amplitudes it returns. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"PauliStabilizer", "[", "qs", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c0245a5d-64a8-41de-b430-60de2b50e201"],
 " converts a state to a tableau, succeeds only on stabilizer states, and \
records the global phase it finds. Because the phase is recorded, converting \
a state to a tableau and back returns the same physical state including its \
global phase; the reverse round trip returns the same stabilizer group, \
though not necessarily the same generator list. The conversions keep the \
phase; only the Clifford gate updates inside the tableau act up to global \
phase."
}], "Text",
 CellID->49659130,ExpressionUUID->"46567f11-decf-44bf-b4d7-5d8e4b7d7048"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The boundary is sharp. Clifford gates, including the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c4557cff-58ea-4402-8906-5d634c20262c"],
 " phase gate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c376322e-76a3-4add-9c02-63787a14b48b"],
 ", keep the tableau. A non-Clifford phase gate such as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "86ae0c61-721a-433c-886b-15f34609a872"],
 " leaves it for a sum of stabilizer states. A non-Clifford non-phase unitary \
is refused."
}], "Text",
 CellID->464508221,ExpressionUUID->"673d26e5-fe1c-4615-b602-458bc01d7347"],

Cell["\<\
A separate result connects the two representations in odd dimension; it \
concerns qudit states, not the qubit tableau above. A pure qudit state has a \
nonnegative discrete Wigner function exactly when it is a stabilizer state. \
So Wigner negativity appears only once a state leaves the stabilizer set. It \
appears only on states that a non-Clifford gate actually moves: a gate \
diagonal in the computational basis fixes its own stabilizer eigenstates, and \
those stay nonnegative. Qubits are even-dimensional, and there Wigner \
nonnegativity is not this criterion.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1361313038,ExpressionUUID->"a4264537-3d72-4508-929f-3ee1918ca030"],

Cell["9. Execution methods", "Section",
 CellID->1907680634,ExpressionUUID->"dd2dc0d6-b513-4579-abcd-3ef7a6b5b0e8"],

Cell["\<\
A circuit is a diagram until a method turns it into a value, and the methods \
do not all return the same kind of value. The default method contracts the \
circuit as one network of tensors joined at its wires, in a chosen order. The \
Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger method instead multiplies the gates one at a time. \
The stabilizer method runs in the tableau. These are exact simulators: each \
must return, after decoding, the state the circuit's operator produces, so on \
any one circuit they must agree. An external method hands the circuit to a \
simulator or to hardware, and there the return is not a state but what the \
backend gives back: a table of shot counts, or a job to be queried. The exact \
methods agree on the output state; a shot-based or hardware run returns \
samples of it, not the state.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->483148123,ExpressionUUID->"f666d727-fd7e-402b-94c6-23ddb85fd159"],

Cell["10. Distances and entanglement", "Section",
 CellID->1195452142,ExpressionUUID->"991d01aa-fc50-45d8-bea4-692a636bf406"],

Cell["\<\
Two families read a number off the density-matrix representation rather than \
build a new object.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1521685512,ExpressionUUID->"d6aae513-8bb7-4ed2-855b-384c2a85bd27"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A distance compares two states. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumDistance", "[", 
   RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "b"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f8b42584-d5ed-4daf-9d8b-4ab7a4818c01"],
 " defaults to the ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Fidelity\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d77bf612-f148-4049-b466-7cae08bbbadc"],
 " measure. Despite the name this measure is a distance, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "-", 
   StyleBox["Re",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["a", "TI"]], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["b", "TI"]]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aa357f5a-9cd3-4c22-8833-972779a94235"],
 ", zero on identical states and not the Uhlmann fidelity itself. A third \
argument selects another measure instead: trace, Bures, Bures-angle, \
Hilbert-Schmidt, relative-entropy, relative-purity, or Bloch. ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumSimilarity"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f921dd45-1daa-4762-858e-b3fb5d5372ca"],
 " is the companion quantity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "-", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aed23aed-75ad-4d33-9e8d-e6f839bf4c84"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->97201263,ExpressionUUID->"16c281d6-6804-4c41-9aaf-cec3e2e60e35"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An entanglement monotone reads one state across a bipartition. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumEntanglementMonotone", "[", 
   RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "part"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49a030bd-107d-4115-8742-96b182ac54c9"],
 " defaults to the concurrence, taken from the reduced state for a pure input \
and from the concurrence vector for a mixed one, and exact only for two \
qubits or a pure state. Its alternatives are negativity, log-negativity, the \
entanglement and Renyi entropies, realignment, mutual information, and \
discord. ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumEntangledQ"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bbdd0f92-df0b-4a79-ba1f-f7b2270ba581"],
 " tests entanglement and defaults to the realignment criterion."
}], "Text",
 CellID->878831761,ExpressionUUID->"017a020a-5191-44ee-bd06-5e82327fd123"],

Cell["\<\
All of these are functionals on the state already represented, so they \
inherit its shape assumptions. Nothing here checks that the input is \
normalized or positive.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1048559713,ExpressionUUID->"b479fc59-4421-4ada-9d5f-90f19152f339"],

Cell["11. Assumptions and limitations", "Section",
 CellID->300048012,ExpressionUUID->"df368ed9-5969-4446-bd98-3e268442efb7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "QF checks shapes, not physics. A constructor accepts a vector or a square \
matrix of the right dimension; it does not check normalization, positivity, \
unitarity, or trace preservation, which are assumptions of the model, \
readable afterward but not enforced. So a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumState"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08a27477-2271-4b26-9e91-d0e3c8406f37"],
 " need not be normalized, and a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumChannel"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a176260b-31c0-4894-93da-7cb318961fda"],
 " need not preserve the trace."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1962937852,ExpressionUUID->"74a04e17-b504-4092-8214-85b7ac4d1947"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two operations are computed directly on the coefficient matrix in the \
declared basis, and each matches the physical operation only under a \
condition. The adjoint conjugate-transposes the coefficient matrix, which is \
the Hermitian adjoint ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "99c5ab3b-236d-4ba4-a2d0-171f3c692a73"],
 ", fixed by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
       StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]}]},
    "BraKet"], "=", 
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
       StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "BraKet"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8ade59cc-ffa5-44d6-a98b-3be66ded7a0f"],
 ", only in an orthonormal basis; in a non-orthonormal basis the overlaps of \
the basis vectors, collected in the Gram matrix, enter, and the bare \
conjugate-transpose omits them. The partial trace contracts a subsystem's \
output index with its input index, and because the trace of an operator does \
not depend on the basis, this reproduces the physical partial trace ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Tr",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["S", "TI"]], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], "\[CenterDot]", 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{
       StyleBox["i", "TI"]},
      "Bra"], "\[CenterDot]", 
     TemplateBox[{
       StyleBox["i", "TI"]},
      "Ket"]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07f49e36-b505-4a8f-ac41-d77ecd59b619"],
 " whenever the subsystem's two sides carry the same basis; when they carry \
different bases the contraction pairs vectors that are not dual to each \
other, and the result is not the trace. In both cases QF still returns a \
well-defined object, but off these conditions it is not the physical adjoint \
or partial trace."
}], "Text",
 CellID->588230824,ExpressionUUID->"0970dc82-d8e9-40a5-961b-457441412de5"],

Cell["\<\
Two identifications must not be over-read. Two kets that differ by a phase \
are the same physical state, and two normalized density matrices equal as \
operators are the same state; the freedom to rescale an unnormalized positive \
operator to unit trace is a chosen normalization, not a general equality of \
QF objects. In particular a subnormalized measurement branch is not \
identified up to an arbitrary positive factor, because its trace is its \
probability. And the finite-dimensional compositional core described here \
does not exhaust the kernel: the bosonic and second-quantization layers carry \
their own objects and are outside this account.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2099309037,ExpressionUUID->"ea7af6bb-0d40-40a9-bc30-5c533cf06aef"],

Cell["Appendix A. Objects and their nesting", "Section",
 CellID->512383039,ExpressionUUID->"d5964f60-bc24-4e66-a11b-6c7b3cacb956"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The heads wrap one another; there is no second data structure in the chain. \
A ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f4e21b7c-46dc-45da-a08c-9de434790cae"],
 " contains a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumState"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f8a6ac6a-2aef-4889-a06a-a208cf00ee81"],
 "; a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumChannel"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f156461-780a-4963-9b47-83a9a1060774"],
 " and a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumMeasurementOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a2ab85d3-5a52-4282-8a7b-f2f8f22a9c66"],
 " contain a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34ef223e-9971-42b4-947f-4cafc921adbf"],
 "; a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumMeasurement"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "eb6dc4f7-43c6-4d94-b2e2-71e27bc00ff7"],
 " contains a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumMeasurementOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "603e8040-c848-4a2f-bc67-04b99b100295"],
 " after application. The stabilizer heads (",
 Cell[BoxData["PauliStabilizer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "eebb70aa-3b6c-4c61-bf7b-bc1a5eba3c8b"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["StabilizerFrame"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9c0d67f5-1884-45f8-b8ff-d20cbf28735d"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["CliffordChannel"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6a3abeef-3ddc-4e7e-9a09-4c58b81c1fd3"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["GraphState"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05c55ad9-a5bb-4497-bf5b-074deabfd3fe"],
 ") are the one other representation, joined to the tensor representation by \
two conversions."
}], "Text",
 CellID->273308241,ExpressionUUID->"fe601add-ac55-4f57-9104-00b3bd6da4c2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The head that comes back from each call, run against the working tree. A \
lowercase name stands for any object of the matching head: ",
 Cell[BoxData["qs"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57cf5e7b-02f9-4779-9a44-1b7d38a68ee4"],
 " a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumState"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "803d2ae7-afbe-42b5-8dcf-56d4b1db55b9"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["qo"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b181a1e4-ec84-4a09-b3e6-7ad8da1b269e"],
 " a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "dd1a3d48-e2e9-434c-b0ea-234300099c09"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["qmo"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e813c4e8-7a88-49a5-9857-67d7f0260ad4"],
 " a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumMeasurementOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b634d7d-ebc2-4bad-a71e-a5df73226f8a"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["qm"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e0f2c920-abb5-40cd-89ca-649b40dc3e3b"],
 " a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumMeasurement"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "db8966b4-75f2-4e5c-a893-4bb1b2b659ba"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["chan"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8466439e-0796-45c3-a9c1-4a6c503e59da"],
 " a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumChannel"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2aacca00-ff2d-4740-a7d4-13682d4f8c70"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["qco"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b5de8d31-5091-448f-829e-49cf16ce7fd9"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["qc"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "570c9397-6c85-47d0-8c4f-725bc4b0a3dc"],
 " a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumCircuitOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10acca47-bbbd-4f34-b35f-22dec1f2417d"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData["ps"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11d644ef-a3f4-43c8-9d72-77befcb6f125"],
 " a ",
 Cell[BoxData["PauliStabilizer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d616fd65-18bc-4e27-bb69-70b081acd9d8"],
 "; ",
 Cell[BoxData["op"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fb0a75e-d993-43ce-88ee-c9f4809dcdc6"],
 " is any operation a circuit can hold."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1809098798,ExpressionUUID->"5d2db493-fe98-4ab1-93c2-0bcad5fd6d58"],

