 CellID->156430199,ExpressionUUID->"0b2b76f4-85a5-431d-8416-02c6c4981117"],

Cell["Appendix B. Constructor edge cases and wire numbers", "Section",
 CellID->724760089,ExpressionUUID->"232d607a-738c-4885-afce-dc60d05cc22c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The integer on each wire records its role by its sign: a positive number is \
a live quantum wire; a non-positive number is a trace subsystem inside a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumChannel"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8d46b760-cc30-462b-b316-22e77480a57c"],
 " and an outcome subsystem inside a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumMeasurementOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "708daa72-f4b6-46a3-aebf-b37261a62706"],
 ", and carries no role on a bare operator. The role is assigned by the \
wrapper, so the same coefficients serve as a unitary, a channel, or a \
measurement, and the role is invisible in a bare wire list."
}], "Text",
 CellID->168408080,ExpressionUUID->"94fa2c99-146e-470d-a3bb-3d7945480000"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "When an operator reaches wires the state does not fill, the state is padded \
with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "010a8451-3cbf-4ad5-922c-5794d85d3022"],
 " on the missing wires, up to the full input order of the one-element \
circuit, gaps included; the padding is by qubits, so a missing qutrit fails \
with a dimension message rather than being prepared. A coefficient array \
whose dimension factors, such as six, is split into subsystems by default (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Range", "[", "6", "]"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d5df660a-b827-4e8f-9f13-305c35d2adb1"],
 " is a qubit and a qutrit, not one six-level qudit); pass the dimension \
explicitly to override. A tableau is stored bit-packed, sixty-two qubits to a \
machine word, with one recorded global phase (the sixty-two-rows-per-word \
layout is a transient packing used only by the compiled gate fold)."
}], "Text",
 CellID->811283638,ExpressionUUID->"e9c43035-583c-42fd-a398-1837dbf93e1a"],

Cell["Appendix C. Phase-space formulas", "Section",
 CellID->207978548,ExpressionUUID->"64b6c4dd-e395-45f9-9258-b739f893a84b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In odd dimension the Wigner basis element at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["q", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "87cc3df2-7b83-4901-80b5-22e6d4c2b4d7"],
 " is a displaced parity, built from three operators on a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f445ad4b-d980-424a-bfb1-229e298b27e6"],
 "-level system with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], "/", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "caf3c343-c8ea-44e1-917d-8c8c1bd95377"],
 ": the Fourier operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", 
     SqrtBox[
      StyleBox["d", "TI"]]], 
    RowBox[{
     UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
      StyleBox["j", "TI"],
      LimitsPositioning->False], 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[
        RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]], 
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["j", "TI"]},
       "Ket"]}]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a6e4a47d-1a88-4d01-a753-c72d019eeff0"],
 ", the clock ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e8a28449-88f0-4fc2-bf96-e4e488bfe9d6"],
 ", and the shift ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], "-", "1", 
       StyleBox["mod", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"]}]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8f3c4cd5-d278-45ad-a273-0b7401724977"],
 ". The parity is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b0c49646-0bfd-40c7-9b0c-b9072e49526e"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["F", "TI"], "2"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["mod", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"]}]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7cdb4c7e-0377-4b87-a905-88babe367930"],
 ", and the displaced parity is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["q", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[Pi]", 
     StyleBox["q", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "/", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["F", "TI"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["q", "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e592e6b8-9c39-4d51-af3c-bcbc712adf4f"],
 ", which the kernel builds directly in this form rather than through a \
separate displacement operator. The Wigner basis element at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["q", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aa65abad-7ade-4bd3-b353-c6dbad5971fb"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["q", "TI"]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["p", "TI"]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ad9fc900-43fd-434f-a71e-6de5e007b0ff"],
 ", reaching every grid point because ",
 Cell[BoxData["2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e593c4b-972b-48d3-83ef-0d036052eb4b"],
 " is invertible mod ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9d2d9ec4-3942-4e94-bc95-fec229f9ee80"],
 "; the elements are Hermitian, unit trace, mutually orthogonal with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["a", "TI"]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["b", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"a", "b"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bc6e521-d057-4ce9-a851-5a15a35f7c1e"],
 ", summing to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "\[CenterDot]", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b0bc5f3d-0c96-45a4-b863-a9fb952b3085"],
 ", and the coordinates are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["q", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["q", "TI"]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["p", "TI"]}]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bea4f6c5-b3d4-4a07-a53a-8d7921f9a715"],
 ". In even dimension ",
 Cell[BoxData["2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ef0b0fe5-49a5-4b2d-add1-265de5a72c38"],
 " is not invertible, the parity orbit is too small, and the element is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["q", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d5f7cee-89a8-4cd0-8a4f-665a48fda14d"],
 " instead, with Gram matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "\[CenterDot]", 
   StyleBox["I", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "99d83264-21be-469a-8caf-e565565f8f2b"],
 "; for a qubit these are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"2", "{", 
    StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], ",", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "017ea0b8-3af2-4f77-9ab7-ffa6b44687f7"],
 ". The elements no longer share a trace, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a5778a-8831-443e-bdcd-29f35feae360"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "598a4dfc-c81f-4edc-8515-472af0efb8d4"],
 ", which for a qubit is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "0"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8140001a-2b64-440a-882f-5826fac5edcd"],
 ". The inverse ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumWeylTransform"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "22b79637-6ca5-4da8-9ca7-b86fef6c3da1"],
 " takes the square root of each dimension (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"9", "\[Rule]", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "122f0a5b-fe02-45d3-b9d4-5b05bfa5e23b"],
 " for a qutrit)."
}], "Text",
 CellID->437474228,ExpressionUUID->"173902e6-ef66-4e14-8589-7c08aefb9c07"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The rate matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"HamiltonianTransitionRate", "[", "H", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "87db6deb-41e0-4d2a-a1c4-4a9ba214b6cf"],
 " is the matrix of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], ",", "\[CenterDot]"}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ff997b6-f0a7-4ba9-b6e6-11fe399c3a97"],
 " in these coordinates with no further factor. Trace preservation is the \
weighted condition ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fabc5f2-47c4-49ba-b3fe-1bd92ad16367"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c6e27395-3b6a-4c4c-a796-97ae431250c7"],
 ", since ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9e4b1d67-6098-4adb-9077-7586e24affd7"],
 "; it holds for a valid generator. The ordinary column sums ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["1",
     FontWeight->"Bold",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cc6c5920-0199-441f-b408-ee784c3f9352"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["1",
   FontWeight->"Bold",
   FontSlant->"Plain"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f33a625d-d0c0-4bfc-89d7-d28be800806e"],
 " the all-ones vector, are a different quantity. When all basis elements \
share one nonzero trace, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "\[Proportional]", 
   StyleBox["1",
    FontWeight->"Bold",
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75b1ffda-5163-4eb0-8093-469fa5df1107"],
 ", so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["1",
     FontWeight->"Bold",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a7cb942d-343e-4b5d-8377-d79ba7a5fb29"],
 " is proportional to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8f2cb0ac-8f53-4556-9d85-01d226f7da06"],
 " and vanishes, as for the odd-dimension displaced parities (zero for the \
qutrit); with unequal traces it need not, and the even-dimension qubit basis \
has ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["1",
     FontWeight->"Bold",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["R", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["h", "TI"]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", "2", 
     StyleBox["h", "TI"]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d07827e-c193-4fa5-9b89-08d8424c08d4"],
 " for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25b0d4d0-096f-484e-b6bb-b95adc02292b"],
 ". The sign-sector transform ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumPositiveTransform"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "861b2c4d-6322-4009-bd8e-c4f8ae61bdef"],
 " splits the coordinate axis into a nonnegative pair ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["w", "TI"], "+"], ",", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["w", "TI"], "-"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d9455f12-bbaf-4389-9dbd-2a0a2c7b2623"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["w", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["w", "TI"], "+"], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["w", "TI"], "-"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54a11409-eeaa-4690-8667-9d29791a4d85"],
 "; on a matrix it yields the block form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["T", "TI"], "+"], ",", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["T", "TI"], "-"]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["T", "TI"], "-"], ",", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["T", "TI"], "+"]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c0223fc-e30f-4718-af89-cecbdd09ef38"],
 ", and the decoding ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], ",", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["I", "TI"]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "32417ad1-c9c3-461f-83cc-912ce60f3cb8"],
 " satisfies ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CapitalDelta]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a51571c4-175c-4c64-bcf3-080898cae947"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->874582697,ExpressionUUID->"46040b61-e1e4-453b-8961-250e44eb9585"],

Cell["Appendix D. Related work", "Section",
 CellID->11631581,ExpressionUUID->"2d86e240-8653-4825-a51e-154597126bc2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The nearest published model for QF is a composite: a categorical process \
model with an environment and classical structure as the meaning, and a \
Proto-Quipper-style typed core as the language. The categorical line [Abr04, \
Sel07, Coe06, Coe10, Coe14] is the closest reading of the channels and \
measurements: the doubling ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Bend\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35305d2c-567e-40d0-8776-1ada9af85c03"],
 " corresponds to the completely positive maps (CPM) construction, the cup \
and cap to a dagger-compact structure, the spiders to basis structures, and a \
measurement to a morphism to a classical object. The programming-language \
line [Rio17, Fu22, Pay17, Sel04, Sel04b, Ros26] is the closest reading of the \
circuit shape: a circuit as a morphism in a free category with a functor for \
its meaning. The operator-algebraic line [Cho14, Jia21, Lin25c, Ran21] is \
where the picture structure lives, the Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger description \
evolving states and the Heisenberg description evolving observables. Phase \
space is Wootters and Gross [Woo87, Gro06, Gib04], the rate matrix is Braasch \
and Wootters [Bra20], and the tableau is Aaronson and Gottesman [Aar04, \
Got98, Nes09]."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1933762060,ExpressionUUID->"91b90eff-546a-43ce-be8b-a0b7a019df19"],

Cell["\<\
Against that composite, QF combines four things no surveyed system combines: \
a basis stored with every state and operator, with an implicit change of \
basis rather than a rejection (Qwerty [Ada24] and D\[IAcute]az-Caro [Dia25b, \
Dia25] put the basis in the type instead; D\[IAcute]az-Caro's core carries an \
implicit change of basis of its own, but in the type rather than stored with \
the object); three pictures in one object model, connected by transforms, \
with the phase-space picture unrepresented in any surveyed system; channels \
stored as a Stinespring operator with the environment as trace subsystems; \
and a second representation, the stabilizer tableau, joined by conversions \
that carry the global phase. Yao.jl [Luo19] shares the unified block type but \
has none of the four; the idealized cores lambda-Q# [Sin22], QIR [Luo23], and \
Qunity [Voi22] formalize a designed subset rather than a shipping framework.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1055776787,ExpressionUUID->"668d0185-c33f-4fd6-a2bc-3433fbc67434"],

Cell["\<\
This comparison records what each cited work builds into its published model, \
not a limit of its approach: a feature a work does not present may be a \
matter of scope rather than reach, since for a designed core or a categorical \
axiomatization the construction could often be added within the same \
framework. It is a comparison against published formal models; coexisting \
statevector and stabilizer representations with conversions between them are \
also routine in circuit simulators such as Stim, Qiskit Aer, and Cirq, so \
what is distinctive in QF is not that the two coexist but that they form one \
object model, with the phase-carrying round trip stated as a property.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1859711813,ExpressionUUID->"a0fbbaec-269e-4815-b6b6-ed6b6152ae7e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A vocabulary note, since this appendix speaks the language of the works it \
cites. A ",
 StyleBox["functor", "TI"],
 " is a representation-to-representation map that preserves composition, of \
the kind this account calls a transform; a ",
 StyleBox["morphism", "TI"],
 " is a linear map, channel, or state; a ",
 StyleBox["dagger-compact category", "TI"],
 " is finite-dimensional states and operators with tensor product and \
adjoint; the ",
 StyleBox["CPM construction", "TI"],
 " is the doubling; a ",
 StyleBox["Frobenius algebra", "TI"],
 ", or ",
 StyleBox["spider", "TI"],
 ", is the copy-and-compare structure of a basis."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1348896709,ExpressionUUID->"1ca3c526-a52c-4505-949f-56457a6fa11d"],

